# Keep junk and bulky artifacts out of the build context / image. The production Dockerfile
# copies only src/ (+ requirements.txt) and Dockerfile.test additionally copies tests/ +
# scripts/ + pytest.ini + .coveragerc, so most of this is belt-and-braces.
#
# Two things are deliberately NOT ignored, and each has bitten a build somewhere:
#   * tests/ and scripts/  — the tester image needs them in its build context.
#   * .coveragerc          — it is COPYed into the tester image; ignoring it would silently
#                            fall back to coverage.py's defaults and measure the wrong tree.
# Patterns below are listed by name rather than as `*.md` so adding a doc never accidentally
# knocks one of the above out of the context.
#
# nginx/ is not listed here at all, and the correction is worth making explicitly because C1's
# version of this comment claimed it was exempted "because the load-balancer config is bind-mounted
# from the build context". It is not: `.dockerignore` filters what is sent to the DAEMON for a
# build, and the `lb` service runs the stock `nginx:alpine` image with no build stanza whatsoever.
# `./nginx/nginx.conf:/etc/nginx/nginx.conf:ro` is a bind mount read from the host filesystem at
# container start, which this file cannot affect in either direction. So there is nothing to
# exempt and nothing to add — and it stays out of both images' contexts, which is correct: the
# production image COPYs only src/ and would never use it.

# VCS / planning docs
.git
.gitignore
README.md
plan.md
project_requirements.md

# Python caches / build artifacts
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
build
dist
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv
venv
env
ENV

# Secrets / env — a real .env must never be baked into an image layer. Compose reads it at run
# time via `env_file`, which is the correct seam. The template is exempted explicitly: it holds
# only placeholder values (which Settings rejects on purpose) and is useful documentation inside
# the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local data (Redis dumps, exported counters, scratch results). Redis persistence lives in a
# named volume, never in the build context.
data/
dump.rdb
appendonly.aof
appendonlydir/

# OS / logs
.DS_Store
*.log
